          "For arc summaries, aim for **about 400 words per numbered chapter**, normally **350–450 words**, so chapters across the five arcs have comparable reading lengths. Count story prose only, excluding headings, footnotes, navigation and unnumbered prologues or epilogues. Add supported scene detail to shorter chapters and condense incidental mechanics or repetition in longer ones; do not invent events or add filler to meet the range. Preserve the eight-chapter structure and source footnotes. See the [chapter prose balance report](../reports/NARRATIVE_PROSE_BALANCE_2026-10-24.md).",
          "For completed arc narratives, use **about 400 story words per numbered chapter**, normally **350–450 words**, as a **reading-weight diagnostic rather than a quota**. Count story prose only, excluding headings, footnotes, navigation and unnumbered prologues or epilogues. Add supported scene detail where useful and condense incidental mechanics or repetition; never invent events or add filler to meet the range. Preserve consequential choices, causal connections and necessary aftermath when a chapter needs more space. **Arc boundaries and chapter counts belong to the selected campaign’s approved or implemented chapter maps**, not to a shared five-arc or eight-chapter rule. Preserve source footnotes. For Delvers, follow the [implemented three-arc chapter maps](DELVERS_NARRATIVE_CHAPTER_MAPS.md); the older [chapter prose balance report](../reports/NARRATIVE_PROSE_BALANCE_2026-10-24.md) documents an earlier campaign-specific application, not a universal structure."
